trigger.description:
Trigger object (the automation's root). Always include triggerSlug. Supported shapes:
- Media analyzed in folder(s): { type: "folders", triggerSlug: "media_analyzed", folderIds: string[] (min 1) }
- Inbound webhook (receive external payloads): { type: "folders", triggerSlug: "inbound_webhook", webhookId? (from provision_inbound_webhook; omit to auto-provision a new one on create), childKey? (dot-path narrowing which part of the payload feeds the automation, e.g. "data") }. The create/update response includes inboundWebhook.inboundUrl — the public URL to POST payloads to.
- Custom field updated: { type: "folders", triggerSlug: "field_updated", values: string[] (watched custom field ids, min 1), fieldValueMatches?: [{ fieldId, values: string[] }] (fire only when the field changes TO one of these values; empty values = any change), fieldMatchLogic?: "AND"|"OR" (how multiple fieldValueMatches combine, default "OR") }
- Third-party app event (pull: something in a connected app starts the automation and can bring a file into Speak): { type: "composio", provider: "composio", app, triggerSlug, connectedAccountId, triggerConfig? }. Use any app and trigger slug that list_automation_triggers returns; triggerConfig fills that trigger's configSchema. A trigger marked fileBearing hands a file to the steps: start the steps with a speak-upload step using sourceMode "file" to import it as a recording. New-email triggers (Gmail, Outlook) need at least one filter (from, subjectContains, or the advanced Gmail query); audio and video attachments are imported as recordings (importAttachments, default true) and the email body is saved as a text note only when saveBodyAsNote is true. The app is watched only while the automation is on. A trigger that is checked on a schedule (call, meeting and survey apps such as Aircall, Quo or Gong) cannot be combined with Or triggers. Imports use credits like uploads; credits are checked when the automation is created switched on, turned on, or saved with changed triggers while it stays on, and one automation imports at most 50 files an hour; extra items wait for the next hour. If the connection expires the automation turns off, and items that arrive while it is off are not imported.
Notes: "tags"/"keywords" trigger types are rejected for graph automations. The server stores inbound-webhook triggers with type "webhook" internally — send type "folders" plus the slug as shown above.
